Do not run the video progress meter with no video info

kernel_bootstrap_thread() calls initialize_screen(NULL, kPEAcquireScreen) right
after STARTUP_SUB_EARLY_BOOT -- the first thing past E16.  With a NULL
boot_vinfo the whole mapping block is skipped, so all that call can do is
vc_progress_set() and gc_enable(): the Apple-logo progress meter, for a video
console this port does not use (the injected blob draws the panel).

E16 is the last line on the panel and the next mark never prints, which puts the
stop inside that call.  When vinfo has no depth there is no video console to
acquire, so mark the screen acquired and return.
---
diff --git a/osfmk/console/video_console.c b/osfmk/console/video_console.c
index 384118e..c211958 100644
--- a/osfmk/console/video_console.c
+++ b/osfmk/console/video_console.c
@@ -2941,6 +2941,19 @@ initialize_screen(PE_Video * boot_vinfo, unsigned int op)
 			break;
 		}
 
+		/*
+		 * nio: called from kernel_bootstrap_thread() with a NULL boot_vinfo, so
+		 * there is nothing to map and the only work left is the progress meter
+		 * (vc_progress_set).  This port draws its console with the injected blob,
+		 * not with this video console, and the meter is where the boot stopped --
+		 * right after E16, before the first kernel_bootstrap_log() past EARLY_BOOT.
+		 * With no video info, mark the screen acquired and leave it alone.
+		 */
+		if (vinfo.v_depth == 0) {
+			gc_acquired = TRUE;
+			break;
+		}
+
 		vc_progress_options = vc_user_options;
 		bzero(&vc_user_options, sizeof(vc_user_options));
 
